  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From Field to Thread A Sustainable Fashion Initiative Grown by Women&apos;s Hands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to economically and socially empower women by upcycling agricultural waste, specifically barley straw, into high-quality sustainable products. It focuses on enhancing the design and production capacities of women and their NGOs/cooperatives, while introducing these eco-friendly products to niche markets. Strategic partnerships with high-segment brands will further boost market access and global visibility.</narrative>
  </description>
